ail":"當期 ROA = 1.3%"},{"id":2,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"營業現金流 CFO > 0","passed":1,"detail":"自由現金流 = $623M"},{"id":3,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"資產回報率持續擴張 (ΔROA > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"回報率穩步領先同業基準"},{"id":4,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"應計利潤品質高 (CFO > 淨利潤)","passed":0,"detail":"真實現金流充沛，無虛報帳面獲利"},{"id":5,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"財務槓桿未惡化 (ΔLeverage ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"總負債資產比率 = 41.5%"},{"id":6,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"短期流動性安全 (ΔLiquidity > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"流動比率 = 1.98"},{"id":7,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"股本未遭稀釋 (ΔShares ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"未大幅增發新股割韭菜"},{"id":8,"category":"營運效率","desc":"毛利率擴張 (ΔMargin > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"產品定價權增強，毛利結構健康"},{"id":9,"category":"營運效率","desc":"資產週轉率提升 (ΔTurnover > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"每單位資產產出效益改善"}],"fair_val":8.42,"default_fair_val":8.42,"premium_pct":530.9,"is_undervalued":false,"pe_trailing":17.3,"pe_forward":15.2,"pb_trailing":0.4,"pb_forward":0.4,"div_yield":3.55,"ps_ratio":6.6,"fcf_to_ev":2.25,"fcf_to_mcap":3.8,"liab_to_assets":41.5,"cash_to_assets":13,"current_ratio":1.98,"roe":2.6,"roa":1.3,"moat":{"ticker":"PKX","period":"2026Q2","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":4,"comment_zh":"POSCO Holdings 作為韓國最大的鋼鐵製造商，其品牌在國內市場具有一定的認可度，但鋼鐵產品本質上屬於大宗商品，品牌溢價空間有限。定價權主要受全球供需、原材料成本及宏觀經濟環境影響，而非單純的品牌效應。與其他國際鋼鐵巨頭相比，POSCO 在品牌差異化上的優勢不夠突出，難以形成顯著的定價壁壘。","comment_en":"POSCO Holdings, as South Korea's largest steelmaker, has some brand recognition domestically. However, steel products are fundamentally commodities, limiting significant brand premium potential. Pricing power is primarily dictated by global supply/demand, raw material costs, and macroeconomic conditions, rather than brand alone. Compared to other global steel giants, POSCO's brand differentiation is not strong enough to create a substantial pricing barrier."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":5,"comment_zh":"鋼鐵行業的技術壁壘主要體現在生產工藝的效率和環保標準上。POSCO 在高強度鋼、汽車用鋼等領域擁有一定的技術專利和研發能力，這有助於其在特定細分市場保持競爭力。然而，核心的鋼鐵冶煉技術相對成熟，且全球範圍內存在多家技術領先的競爭對手。監管政策（如環保法規、貿易壁壘）對行業影響較大，但 POSCO 並未展現出獨特的、可持續的監管套利或特許經營優勢。","comment_en":"Technological barriers in the steel industry mainly lie in production efficiency and environmental standards. POSCO possesses certain patents and R&D capabilities in areas like high-strength steel and automotive steel, aiding its competitiveness in specific niches. However, core steelmaking technologies are relatively mature, with several technically advanced global competitors. Regulatory policies (e.g., environmental laws, trade barriers) significantly impact the industry, but POSCO does not exhibit unique, sustainable regulatory arbitrage or franchise advantages."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":5,"comment_zh":"對於終端客戶而言，更換鋼鐵供應商通常涉及重新認證、供應鏈調整和潛在的質量風險，這構成了一定的轉換成本。特別是汽車、造船等行業，對鋼材的規格、質量和穩定性要求極高。POSCO 通過長期合作和提供定制化解決方案，在部分客戶群體中建立了穩定的合作關係。然而，若客戶尋求更低的價格或特定性能，更換供應商的可能性依然存在，轉換成本並非絕對的壁壘。","comment_en":"For end-customers, switching steel suppliers typically involves requalification, supply chain adjustments, and potential quality risks, creating some switching costs. Industries like automotive and shipbuilding have stringent requirements for steel specifications, quality, and consistency. POSCO has established stable relationships with certain customer segments through long-term partnerships and customized solutions. However, if customers seek lower prices or specific performance, switching remains a possibility, meaning switching costs are not an absolute barrier."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"鋼鐵行業的網絡效應非常微弱。其商業模式主要基於生產和銷售實物產品，客戶的購買決策更多取決於價格、質量、交貨時間和技術規格，而非其他用戶的使用體驗。POSCO 的業務不依賴於用戶間的互動或數據積累來提升產品價值，因此網絡效應幾乎不存在，無法構成有效的經濟護城河。","comment_en":"Network effects are very weak in the steel industry. The business model is primarily based on producing and selling physical products, with customer purchasing decisions driven by price, quality, delivery time, and technical specifications, rather than user experiences. POSCO's operations do not rely on user interactions or data accumulation to enhance product value, thus network effects are virtually non-existent and do not form a significant economic moat."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"POSCO 作為全球領先的鋼鐵企業之一，擁有顯著的規模經濟優勢。其龐大的生產規模有助於降低單位生產成本，並在採購原材料時獲得更優惠的價格。此外，POSCO 在生產效率、技術研發和全球佈局方面持續投入，不斷優化成本結構。這種規模帶來的成本優勢，使其在價格競爭中處於有利地位，並能更好地抵禦市場波動。","comment_en":"As one of the world's leading steel producers, POSCO benefits from significant economies of scale. Its vast production capacity helps lower per-unit manufacturing costs and provides leverage in raw material procurement. Continuous investment in production efficiency, R&D, and global presence further optimizes its cost structure. This scale-driven cost advantage positions POSCO favorably in price competition and enhances its resilience against market fluctuations."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":4,"comment_zh":"POSCO 在韓國本土擁有領先的市場地位和完善的基礎設施，這構成了一定的地理優勢。其在印尼等地的海外投資也旨在獲取資源和市場份額。然而，鋼鐵行業的競爭是全球性的，優秀的礦產資源和生產基地在全球範圍內均有分佈。POSCO 並不擁有獨一無二、難以複製的地理資產，其優勢更多體現在運營和市場滲透上，而非絕對的地理壟斷。","comment_en":"POSCO holds a leading market position and well-developed infrastructure in South Korea, providing a certain geographical advantage. Overseas investments, such as in Indonesia, aim to secure resources and market share. However, the steel industry is globally competitive, with valuable mineral resources and production bases distributed worldwide. POSCO does not possess unique, irreplicable geographical assets; its advantages stem more from operations and market penetration than absolute geographical monopoly."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"POSCO 在生產效率和技術創新方面長期處於行業領先地位。公司不斷導入先進的生產技術和智能製造系統，以提高產品質量、降低能耗和生產成本。其在綠色鋼鐵和氫能等新興領域的探索，也顯示了其對未來趨勢的把握和運營的靈活性。雖然鋼鐵行業整體競爭激烈，但 POSCO 持續優化運營的能力，使其能夠在複雜的市場環境中保持較高的盈利能力和競爭力。","comment_en":"POSCO has long been a leader in production efficiency and technological innovation within the steel sector. The company consistently adopts advanced manufacturing technologies and smart systems to enhance product quality, reduce energy consumption, and lower production costs. Its exploration into green steel and hydrogen energy demonstrates foresight regarding future trends and operational flexibility. Despite intense industry competition, POSCO's continuous operational optimization enables it to maintain strong profitability and competitiveness in a complex market environment."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"POSCO Holdings 作為控股公司，其資本配置能力對整體價值至關重要。公司在維持鋼鐵主業的競爭力的同時，積極拓展氫能、二次電池材料等新興業務，展現了多元化發展的戰略。然而，過去幾年的 ROE 和 ROA 表現相對平庸，顯示其在資本配置的效率和回報方面仍有提升空間。如何在傳統業務和新興業務之間取得平衡，並確保高資本回報率，是其面臨的挑戰。","comment_en":"As a holding company, POSCO Holdings' capital allocation capability is crucial. While maintaining competitiveness in its core steel business, the company is actively expanding into emerging areas like hydrogen energy and secondary battery materials, indicating a diversification strategy. However, its relatively modest ROE and ROA in recent years suggest room for improvement in capital allocation efficiency and returns. Balancing traditional and new ventures while ensuring high capital returns remains a key challenge."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"POSCO 通過提供高質量、定制化的鋼鐵產品和可靠的供應鏈服務，與眾多汽車、建築和造船行業的客戶建立了長期穩定的合作關係。這種基於產品質量、技術支持和服務的客戶忠誠度，有助於維持較高的客戶留存率。然而，鋼鐵行業的客戶議價能力較強，且市場上存在替代品和競爭者，因此客戶留存並非絕對，仍需持續努力維護。","comment_en":"POSCO fosters long-term, stable relationships with clients in the automotive, construction, and shipbuilding sectors by providing high-quality, customized steel products and reliable supply chain services. This customer loyalty, built on product quality, technical support, and service, contributes to a relatively high retention rate. However, customers in the steel industry often possess significant bargaining power, and market alternatives and competitors exist, meaning retention is not absolute and requires continuous effort."},"m10_durability":{"score":5,"comment_zh":"鋼鐵行業是基礎工業的重要組成部分，需求相對穩定，具有一定的週期性但長期趨勢向上。POSCO 作為行業龍頭，其業務具有一定的持久性。然而，該行業面臨來自新材料的潛在顛覆、環保壓力以及全球經濟波動的風險。POSCO 積極佈局綠色轉型和新興業務，試圖增強其業務的長期韌性，但其核心業務的持久性仍受宏觀經濟和行業週期的影響。","comment_en":"The steel industry is a fundamental part of the economy with relatively stable, albeit cyclical, demand and a long-term upward trend. As an industry leader, POSCO's business possesses a degree of durability. However, it faces potential disruption from new materials, environmental pressures, and global economic volatility. POSCO's strategic moves into green transformation and new ventures aim to enhance long-term resilience, but the durability of its core business remains subject to macroeconomic factors and industry cycles."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"POSCO Holdings 的護城河主要體現在其規模經濟帶來的成本優勢（M5）和持續的運營效率（M7）上，這使其在全球鋼鐵市場中佔據有利地位。其品牌（M1）和轉換成本（M3）提供了一定的保護，但受限於大宗商品的屬性。網絡效應（M4）幾乎不存在。專利與監管（M2）、地理資產（M6）壁壘相對有限。客戶留存（M9）和資本配置（M8）有待加強。總體而言，POSCO 屬於典型的「商品型」或「成本領導型」企業，其護城河相對穩固但並非無懈可擊，易受宏觀經濟週期和行業競爭的影響，缺乏巴菲特所青睞的強大特許經營權或收費橋模式。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"POSCO Holdings' moat primarily stems from its cost advantages derived from economies of scale (M5) and sustained operational efficiency (M7), positioning it well in the global steel market. Brand (M1) and switching costs (M3) offer some protection but are limited by the commodity nature of steel. Network effects (M4) are negligible. Barriers from patents/regulation (M2) and unique geographical assets (M6) are moderate. Customer retention (M9) and capital allocation (M8) require further strengthening. Overall, POSCO is a classic 'commodity' or 'cost-leader' type company. Its moat is solid but not impregnable, susceptible to macroeconomic cycles and industry competition, lacking the strong franchise or toll-bridge characteristics Buffett favors.","evidenceHash":"35aee923d8ba2710a1a21ed0c1add5762fc09ff9556435d4d11d00be080f1bc3","assessmentPolicy":"us-buffett-moat-v3"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null},"fScore":{"score":5,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"distress","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"KRW","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-28T14:24:37.317Z","evidenceHash":"7580131fc837bd6f04cb7d1ad60e9f710c4b7b2e910635793a0fbf166efb6ff8"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"clean","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"KRW","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-28T14:24:37.317Z","evidenceHash":"7580131fc837bd6f04cb7d1ad60e9f710c4b7b2e910635793a0fbf166efb6ff8"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/PKX.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/PKX.png","website":"http://www.posco-inc.com","ceo":"In-Hwa Chang","full_time_employees":"429","description":"POSCO Holdings Inc., a South Korean-based enterprise, operates globally in the production and sale of steel rolled products and plates through its extensive network of subsidiaries. The company’s multifaceted business is structured across four primary segments: Steel, Construction, Trading, and an expansive \"Others\" category. Its steel portfolio features hot and cold rolled steel, steel plates, wire rods, galvanized sheets, electrical steel, stainless steel, and titanium. Beyond its foundational steel operations, POSCO Holdings diversifies into various sectors. Its Construction segment specializes in the design, fabrication, and erection of steel mills and their infrastructure, along with commercial and residential facilities. The Trading division manages the import and export of raw materials, facilitates inter-company supply and procurement, and deals in a wide array of steel products. The comprehensive \"Others\" segment covers a significant breadth of industries. This includes infrastructure and industrial services such as power generation, network and system integration, logistics, cargo handling, and facility maintenance. It engages in resource management and industrial material supply, encompassing resource and mine development, sales of iron ore and coal, fuel cell technologies, refractory materials, and quicklime manufacturing. Real estate operations span development, rental, sales, and management, complemented by architectural design and housing agency services. Furthermore, POSCO Holdings is active in engineering, research and consulting, investment in venture, energy, and technology sectors, e-commerce, and intellectual property services. Its diverse undertakings also extend to IT services, electric control engineering, forest resources development, wastewater treatment, agricultural processing (rice and grain sales), education, and various social enterprise initiatives. Founded in 1968, POSCO Holdings Inc. maintains its headquarters in Pohang, South Korea.","description_en":"POSCO Holdings Inc., a South Korean-based enterprise, operates globally in the production and sale of steel rolled products and plates through its extensive network of subsidiaries. The company’s multifaceted business is structured across four primary segments: Steel, Construction, Trading, and an expansive \"Others\" category. Its steel portfolio features hot and cold rolled steel, steel plates, wire rods, galvanized sheets, electrical steel, stainless steel, and titanium. Beyond its foundational steel operations, POSCO Holdings diversifies into various sectors. Its Construction segment specializes in the design, fabrication, and erection of steel mills and their infrastructure, along with commercial and residential facilities. The Trading division manages the import and export of raw materials, facilitates inter-company supply and procurement, and deals in a wide array of steel products. The comprehensive \"Others\" segment covers a significant breadth of industries. This includes infrastructure and industrial services such as power generation, network and system integration, logistics, cargo handling, and facility maintenance. It engages in resource management and industrial material supply, encompassing resource and mine development, sales of iron ore and coal, fuel cell technologies, refractory materials, and quicklime manufacturing. Real estate operations span development, rental, sales, and management, complemented by architectural design and housing agency services. Furthermore, POSCO Holdings is active in engineering, research and consulting, investment in venture, energy, and technology sectors, e-commerce, and intellectual property services. Its diverse undertakings also extend to IT services, electric control engineering, forest resources development, wastewater treatment, agricultural processing (rice and grain sales), education, and various social enterprise initiatives. Founded in 1968, POSCO Holdings Inc. maintains its headquarters in Pohang, South Korea.","description_zh":"**POSCO Holdings Inc. (PKX) 業務營運概述**\n\nPOSCO Holdings Inc.（浦項控股）為一家總部位於韓國的全球性企業，透過其子公司網絡，專注於鋼鐵軋延品與鋼板的生產及銷售。公司業務結構劃分為四大主要板塊：鋼鐵、營建、貿易及「其他」多元事業。\n\n鋼鐵事業涵蓋熱軋鋼、冷軋鋼、鋼板、線材、鍍鋅鋼板、電磁鋼片、不鏽鋼及鈦金屬等多元產品。營建事業則專精於鋼廠及其基礎設施、商業及住宅設施的設計、製造與施工。貿易事業負責原物料進出口、集團內供應鏈管理及鋼鐵產品的廣泛交易。\n\n「其他」多元事業則橫跨多個領域，包括：發電、網路系統整合、物流、貨物處理、廠房維護等基礎設施與工業服務；資源與礦業開發、鐵礦砂與煤炭銷售、燃料電池技術、耐火材料及生石灰製造等資源管理與工業材料供應；不動產開發、租賃、銷售與管理，以及建築設計與住宅代理服務。此外，公司亦涉足工程、研發諮詢、創投、能源、科技、電子商務、智慧財產權服務、資訊科技、電機工程、森林資源開發、廢水處理、農產品加工（稻米、穀物銷售）、教育及社會企業等多元領域。","address":"POSCO Center","city":"Seoul","state":"NG","zip":"06194","country":"KR","phone":"82 (54) 2200114","full_address":"POSCO Center, Seoul, NG 06194, KR","range_52w":"48.5-92.4","year_high":92.4,"year_low":48.5,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":48.5,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[],"stock_splits":[],"fmp_symbol":"PKX","real_5y_prices":[],"historical_dcf_series":[],"name_en":"POSCO Holdings Inc.","expansion":{"status":"available","capturedAt":"2026-10-22T14:09:24.551Z","reason":null,"detailPath":"cache/us_companies/PKX.json"},"z_score":1.67,"z_score_model":"z","z_score_zone":"distress","z_score_breakdown":[{"id":1,"key":"x1","category":"營運資金","desc":"營運資金 / 總資產 (X1)","desc_en":"Working capital / Total as